From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:32:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Add the ambient light sensor

The iPad Air 2 has a CT819 light sensor, which the tsl2583 driver
serves as on the A7 iPads. Apple's device trees of the J81 and J82
(iPadOS 15.8.8) list it twice on i2c2: als1 at 0x49 with interrupt
GPIO 103 and als2 at 0x29 with interrupt GPIO 110, both
"probe-for-hardware", so iOS uses the one that answers. Describe both;
the absent one fails its chip ID read.

Both nodes name the unit's SysCfg LSCI record (syscfg/LSCI/0xC8) as
alsCalibration. Point als0 and als1 at them so that the loader copies
the record into each.

i2c2 has nothing else described and is enabled for the sensor. The
interrupt flags follow the ADT's (1, as on the PMU line, which is
level-low); the driver polls and does not request the interrupt.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index 7588f53..0db7a74 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
 	chassis-type = "tablet";
 
 	aliases {
+		als0 = &als49;	/* the loader copies the ADT's alsCalibration here */
+		als1 = &als29;	/* the same record, for the sensor at 0x29 */
 		bluetooth0 = &bluetooth;
 		serial3 = &serial3;
 		touchscreen0 = &touchscreen;
@@ -264,6 +266,33 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The ambient light sensor: a CT819 on i2c2. The device trees of the J81
+ * and J82 list it twice, as i2c2/als1 at 0x49 (interrupt GPIO 103) and
+ * i2c2/als2 at 0x29 (interrupt GPIO 110), both "probe-for-hardware": iOS
+ * uses the one that answers. Both are described; the absent one fails its
+ * chip ID read. Both name the unit's SysCfg LSCI record as alsCalibration,
+ * which the loader copies into each through the als0 and als1 aliases.
+ * i2c2 has nothing else on it.
+ */
+&i2c2 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/* m1n1 adds apple,als-calibration from the ADT */
+	als29: light-sensor@29 {
+		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
+		reg = <0x29>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 110 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+
+	/* m1n1 adds apple,als-calibration from the ADT */
+	als49: light-sensor@49 {
+		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
+		reg = <0x49>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 103 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+};
+
 /* SmartIO: the DMA engine of every MCA and of spi1 */
 &sio {
 	status = "okay";
